<surname>Ngugi</surname><given-names>EN</given-names></name><name><surname>Prasada Rao</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name><name><surname>Willbond</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Moses</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Plummer</surname><given-names>FA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Public health. Reducing HIV transmission in developing countries</article-title><source>Science</source><year>2001</year><volume>292</volume><fpage>224</fpage><lpage>225</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11305312</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.1058187</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B4"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lowndes</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Alary</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Meda</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Gnintoungbe</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Mukenge-Tshibaka</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Adjovi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Buve</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Morison</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Laourou</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanhonou</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Anagonou</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of core and bridging groups in the transmission dynamics of HIV and STIs in Cotonou, Benin, West Africa</article-title><source>Sex Transm Infect</source><year>2002</year><volume>78</volume><fpage>i69</fpage><lpage>77</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12083450</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boily</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Lowndes</surname><g